claimed: buffer-drain — Channel.buffer is the other per-element channel consumer and has never been benchmarked at all. channel-drain cut the merge's consumer side 30% by batching the RECEIVE (taking what is already buffered delays nothing, so no flag); buffer's output has exactly the same shape and should inherit it. Add a buffer lane to the benchmark, route it through Drain, measure. Then re-run the WHOLE ChunkFlushBenchmark in one window so the comparison table is one measurement rather than several stitched together.
